<p>Italian authorities recovered 19 bodies and rescued 58 migrants from a disabled inflatable boat south of Lampedusa after an attempted crossing from Libya to Europe, according to rescue officials and reports published on April 1 and April 2. The boat was found about 135 kilometers off the Italian island, inside Libyan search-and-rescue waters. Italy sent a coast guard vessel from Lampedusa after finding no Libyan coast guard or civilian ships nearby. Rescuers then brought the survivors to Lampedusa.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/VpsIMJhrG1w2WUeI51DumtvzB6zHISGgPivhuJfPAvqn-MXr7-9gzrVV6RkqLfd3pdpWnnd_gf-imT73njciMZgEY_bsHXVtBcci1rNUjnxMRYpC61Jqio0AXPUAtNTsWpC5bu7J0lqe6vFqOyqy0JQeOl0L5RmsHM-hwl96Eg' alt='Image from ABC News coverage of the migrant rescue off Lampedusa.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Children aboard: The 58 survivors included five children, a reminder that families as well as adults were on the crossing.</li><li>Hospital treatment: Seven rescued migrants, including two children, were hospitalized in Lampedusa for hypothermia and intoxication from hydrocarbon fumes after reaching the island.</li><li>Return-voyage danger: Coast guard spokesman Roberto D’Arrigo said some migrants may have died while crews transported them back to Lampedusa in waves that reached up to seven meters.</li><li>Images from shore: Photos released by ANSA showed what appeared to be body bags being unloaded from a coast guard vessel onto a quay after the rescue.</li></ul><blockquote>We are deeply saddened by yet another tragic incident in the Mediterranean - UN refugee agency</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Italian coast guard: Coast guard spokesman Roberto D’Arrigo said an Italian reconnaissance plane spotted the drifting boat on Tuesday and that Italy sent a vessel from Lampedusa after finding no Libyan coast guard or civilian ships in the area. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987660/19-migrants-found-dead-by-italian-agency'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Lampedusa mayor Filippo Mannino: Mannino said seven rescued migrants, including two children, were receiving hospital care for hypothermia and intoxication from hydrocarbon fumes after reaching the island. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987660/19-migrants-found-dead-by-italian-agency'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>UN refugee agency: The agency said it was providing immediate support to survivors in Lampedusa after the latest Mediterranean crossing. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987660/19-migrants-found-dead-by-italian-agency'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/italy-recovers-19-bodies-from-migrant-boat-survivors-taken-to-lampedusa'>Italy recovers 19 bodies from migrant boat, survivors taken to Lampedusa</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/italian-coast-guard-finds-19-migrants-dead-rescues-131617532'>Italian coast guard finds 19 migrants dead and rescues 58 from dinghy off Lampedusa</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987660/19-migrants-found-dead-by-italian-agency'>19 migrants found dead by Italian agency</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>